  << /ActualText (Finally\054 the research proposition\056\n\nIs there a way to model social networks as a graph state with weighted edges and using the rich landscape of percolation theory to get insights about the \034architecture of online spaces \050who has access to what\051\035\054 \034moderation \050which users\057forums when moderated will have the biggest effect on the overall climate\051\035\054 and the impact of affordances\077 \n\nFurthermore\054 is there an opening to utilise AI methods to retrieve these inferences quicker\077 Is there a way to train a model to take as input a graph state with transient edge weights \050people identifying more with a certain section\057user\051 and get insights as to when the network will break into smaller\054 disconnected graphs \050echo\055chambers and unhealthy discussion forums\051\077)
